-- title:
--   Descent of ideal invertibility and a tensor identity along an isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $\pi\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of schemes which is an isomorphism, let $\mathcal L$ be a sheaf of modules on $X$, let $I_1,I_2$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $X$ and $J_1,J_2$ such data on $X'$, and assume $I_1.\mathrm{comap}\,\pi = J_1$ and $I_2.\mathrm{comap}\,\pi = J_2$. Assume $J_1$ and $J_2$ are invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible` for ideal sheaf data: for every point $x$ of the scheme there are an affine open $U$ and a section $f\in\Gamma(U)$ with $x$ in the basic open set of $f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g$ of $\Gamma$ on the affine basic open set of $f$ such that the ideal of the ideal sheaf data on that affine basic open set is generated by $g$. Assume finally that the monoidal product of $\pi^{*}\mathcal L$ with $J_2$'s inverse module is isomorphic to $J_1$'s inverse module (the hypothesis is the nonemptiness of the type of such isomorphisms). The conclusion is threefold: $I_1$ is invertible, $I_2$ is invertible, and there exists an isomorphism $\mathcal L \cong I_1.\mathrm{invModule} \otimes I_2.\mathrm{module}$ in $X$-modules, where for ideal sheaf data $I$ the module $I.\mathrm{module}$ is the kernel of the map from the unit sheaf of modules on $X$ to the pushforward along the closed immersion $I.\mathrm{subschemeι}$ of the unit sheaf on the subscheme, and $I.\mathrm{invModule}$ is its internal dual $(\mathrm{ihom}\,I.\mathrm{module}).\mathrm{obj}\,(\mathbb 1)$.
--
--   In divisor language this is the descent, along an isomorphism of schemes, of a reading $\mathcal L\cong\mathcal O(E_1)\otimes\mathcal O(-E_2)$ of a line bundle as the difference of two effective Cartier divisors: the hypotheses are stated on $X'$ and the conclusion on $X$. It is used in the construction of a pair of relative effective Cartier divisors on the modular curve $X_1(p)$ realising a given line bundle as a twist of the Poincaré bundle.
